      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "| $y$ | $2$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ is shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+7\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
